WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.800
We covered the first three steps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.120
Next, we’ll talk about the feature selection&nbsp;
step. In the feature selection step, we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.920
talked about how construct features using&nbsp;
patient event sequences from the HRC data.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.720
In particular, we construct feature&nbsp;
from raw data in the observation window.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.880
If we look closely at the observation window, we&nbsp;
see event sequence data, which are corresponding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:33.440
to different types of clinical events. For&nbsp;
example, diagnosis, symptoms, medications, patient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:39.600
demographics, lab results, and vital signs. We&nbsp;
can construct features from all those events.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.520
However, not all the events are relevant&nbsp;
for predicting a specific target. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.080
goal of feature selection is to find the truly&nbsp;
predictive features to be included in the model.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.720
For example, here are two patient charts. We&nbsp;
can see some features such as demographics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.000
including age, race, and gender, and vital&nbsp;
signs such as blood pressures, and diagnosis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.160
such as diabetes and hypertension. However, in&nbsp;
reality this patient chart is not that simple.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.440
In fact, we can construct a long list&nbsp;
of features over 20,000 features,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.880
from a typical EHR data set. Not all of&nbsp;
this are relevant for predicting a target.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.880
We need to select the ones that are&nbsp;
relevant to the target condition.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.720
For example, if we want to predict heart failure,&nbsp;
maybe those yellow features are relevant.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:35.440
However, for a different condition, such as,&nbsp;
diabetes. Maybe those purple features are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:44.000
relevant. The goal of features selections&nbsp;
is to identify those predictive features.

